==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Dq1.jpg|right|thumb|A [[pas de deux]] of a production of the '''ballet''' ''Don Quixote''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|ballet}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{m|it|balletto||short dance, ballet}}, diminutive form of {{m|it|ballo||ball}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈbæl.eɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bæˈleɪ/|/ˈbæl.eɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|æleɪ|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-ballet.flac|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[classical]] form of [[dance]].
# A [[theatrical]] [[presentation]] of such [[dancing]], usually with [[music]], sometimes in the form of a [[story]].
# The company of persons who perform this dance.
# {{lb|en|music}} A light [[part song]], frequently with a fa-la-la [[chorus]], common among [[Elizabethan]] and [[Italian]] [[Renaissance]] [[composer]]s.
# {{lb|en|heraldry}} A [[bearing]] in [[coat of arms|coats of arms]] representing one or more [[ball]]s, called [[bezant]]s, [[plate]]s, etc., according to colour.

{{Webster 1913}}

